# UI Layer (Bloc & UI) Rule

This rule documents the conventions and best practices for the UI layer in the Mozome Flutter project.

## Scope

- Applies to: `ui/`, `bloc/`, `ui/` directories, and Bloc/UI-related files.

## Topics

- Bloc pattern for state management
- UI widgets and reusable components
- Code generation and snippets (NALS Mobile Brain)
- Bloc event and state conventions
- UI testing and accessibility

## Best Practices

- Use Bloc for all state management (avoid setState)
- Separate business logic from UI components
- Dispose of all Bloc instances properly
- Write widget and integration tests for UI flows
- Implement proper error handling in Bloc event handlers
- Use repository abstractions from domain layer, never directly access data sources
- Follow the unidirectional data flow pattern: UI events → Bloc events → States → UI updates

